\section{Errors that name the hop}

A launch fails in a different place depending on what changed.
A message like [[KeyError: 'id_token']] would leave us guessing, so every
check raises a [[LaunchError]] that carries the number and name of the hop.
The number ties the error to the list above and to the hops that
[[fbf har-shape]] prints.

<<classes>>=
class LaunchError(Exception):
    """A hop of the LTI launch did not look as expected.

    `hop` is the hop number (0--3) and `step` its name, so that the message
    says where the launch broke.
    """

    def __init__(self, hop, step, message):
        self.hop = hop
        self.step = step
        super().__init__(f"hop {hop} ({step}): {message}")
@

Let's verify that the message carries the hop.

<<test functions>>=
def test_launch_error_names_hop():
  error = LaunchError(3, "FBF launch", "no access_token cookie")
  assert str(error) == "hop 3 (FBF launch): no access_token cookie"
  assert error.hop == 3
